        "mission_intent": "We need the systems security engineering team to perform a comprehensive alignment review of our current program management practices against the foundational frameworks referenced in NIST SP 800-160 Volume 1. Specifically, please map our existing security engineering lifecycle activities to the process standards in ISO/IEC/IEEE 15288 and ISO/IEC/IEEE 12207, and identify any gaps where our practices diverge from the entry-level process requirements described therein. Additionally, cross-reference our system architecting approach against the systems-of-systems architecting principles from Maier's work to ensure our decomposition strategy is sound for our federated environment. The review should also assess whether our software assurance curriculum and training pipeline aligns with the SEI's Master of Software Assurance Reference Curriculum competency areas. Please document all findings in a gap analysis report with remediation recommendations, and flag any areas where our resilience engineering posture needs strengthening. We'd like the draft report delivered by end of next month so we can fold findings into the upcoming program milestone review.",
